{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Three- and four-finger strokes on the glass, for the Mac: which stroke is a gesture, and which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture it is. Each input surface feeds one of these with every direct touch, through its stroke"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"observer. The counts below say three; with ","type":"text"},{"code":"chordFingers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 4 read four.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/init(chordFingers:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/armed","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/chordFingers","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/silent"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/cancelled(_:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/down(_:at:time:holding:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/moved(_:to:time:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/otherTouch()","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/up(_:at:time:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/Gesture","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/Output"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumerations","title":"Enumerations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Gestures-and-zoom","title":"Gestures and zoom","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGesture","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGestureResolver","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/GestureShortcuts","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/ZoomStep","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/PinchStepper"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackpadGestures","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A stroke runs from its first touch down to its last touch up. It goes ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"silent","type":"text"}]},{"text":" once three fingers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are down, before any finger has moved ","type":"text"},{"code":"chordTravel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from where it landed and while no button the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"surface pressed is held (the trackpad’s press-and-hold drag), however slowly they came down and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever else rests on the glass. From then until the next stroke’s first touch the surfaces send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it, no pointer motion, click, button or scroll (a tap’s action runs after its touch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has ended, so silence outlasts the last lift). A two-finger scroll that a third finger joins after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moving is never silent and goes on as it always did; a stroke that never has three fingers down is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never silent, so one- and two-finger strokes are exactly what they were.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A silent stroke is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"armed","type":"text"}]},{"text":", one that can become a gesture, when the three fingers that landed last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"came down within ","type":"text"},{"code":"chordWindow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of each other, before any finger moved ","type":"text"},{"code":"chordTravel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with no button","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held, no touch of the stroke cancelled and at most four fingers down. So a thumb resting on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"glass before neither keeps three fingers from arming nor becomes one of them; three fingers placed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slowly are silent and decide nothing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decision comes at the first lift of one of those three (another finger lifting only leaves the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stroke), from their centroid’s net travel since arming, and their spread. A swipe when the centroid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"travelled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swipeDistance"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickDistance"},{"type":"text","text":" while moving at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickSpeed"},{"type":"text","text":" over the last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"flickWindow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), one axis beats the other by "},{"code":"axisRatio","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the fingers moved together: each of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the three at least "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swipeShare"},{"type":"text","text":" of the centroid’s way along the swipe, and no other finger that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moved ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"type":"text","text":" or more) that share or more against it. In a pinch or a spread some digit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"moves against the others, however far the centroid goes (a thumb-led pinch drags it along with","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the thumb). Else a pinch or a spread when the mean distance from the centroid changed by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pinchRatio"},{"type":"text","text":", of the three and every other finger that moved (a thumb pinching with three"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingers); else nothing. At most one decision per stroke; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fingers"},{"type":"text","text":" counts the three and the other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingers that moved, 4 at most. A fifth finger down leaves the stroke silent and deciding nothing;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"touches the system cancels decide nothing. So a swipe taken back before the lift does nothing, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on a Mac, and a four-finger stroke that iPadOS takes for itself (its touches cancelled) never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches the Mac."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure: Foundation and CoreGraphics only, covered by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackpadGesturesTests"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Deterministic: the same touches give the same outputs. Main thread, as the touches come.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HeadwireInput"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackpadGestures","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"TrackpadGestures","externalID":"s:13HeadwireInput16TrackpadGesturesV"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/silent":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"silent"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"title":"silent","abstract":[{"text":"From three fingers down (see above) until the next stroke’s first touch: the surfaces send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/silent","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/silent"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/init(chordFingers:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/init(chordFingers:)","title":"init(chordFingers:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"chordFingers","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a recogniser whose strokes go silent and arm at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordFingers"},{"type":"text","text":" fingers, 3 or 4."}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/init(chordfingers:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/SystemGestureResolver":{"abstract":[{"text":"Which system action a decided trackpad gesture asks for, remembering the view the last one opened.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SystemGestureResolver","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGestureResolver","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemGestureResolver","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/systemgestureresolver","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemGestureResolver","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://HeadwireInput/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Three- and four-finger strokes on the glass, for the Mac: which stroke is a gesture, and which"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture it is. Each input surface feeds one of these with every direct touch, through its stroke","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"observer. The counts below say three; with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordFingers"},{"type":"text","text":" 4 read four."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"TrackpadGestures","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackpadGestures","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TrackpadGestures","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/SystemGesture":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Mac system action that a trackpad gesture or a key row control triggers."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGesture","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemGesture","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemGesture","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/systemgesture","title":"SystemGesture","role":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/cancelled(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancelled"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"cancelled(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The system took a touch (an iPadOS gesture, an alert): nothing is decided for this stroke,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and one that has not armed never will; a silent one stays silent."}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/cancelled(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/cancelled(_:)"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/chordFingers":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/chordfingers","title":"chordFingers","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"chordFingers","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The fingers that silence and arm a stroke."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/chordFingers","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/PinchStepper":{"abstract":[{"text":"Turns a pinch’s continuous scale into zoom steps, one per 25% of scale.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"PinchStepper","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/PinchStepper","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PinchStepper","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/pinchstepper","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PinchStepper","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/ZoomStep":{"abstract":[{"text":"One step of zoom in the frontmost app.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ZoomStep","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/ZoomStep","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ZoomStep","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/zoomstep","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ZoomStep","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/Output":{"title":"TrackpadGestures.Output","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/Output","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Output","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Output","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/output","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/moved(_:to:time:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/moved(_:to:time:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/moved(_:to:time:)","title":"moved(_:to:time:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finger moves."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"moved","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text